# .gitattributes — what a byte means, decided once, before the first commit.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. This tree grew on Windows with mixed endings and nothing
# enforcing either: 46 files are CRLF (SPEC.md, most of src/, most of okf/) and
# the rest are LF (src/utterance/journal.cpp, src/crdt/document.cpp,
# conformance/cases/*.json). Nothing chose that split; it is an accident of
# which editor touched which file on which day.
#
# Left alone, one ordinary `sed -i` rewrites a whole file's endings while
# changing two lines of it, and after the first push that lands as a
# thousand-line diff in somebody else's review, every time, forever. Void
# Hormiga learned this the same way one file at a time.
#
# `text=auto` settles it: git stores text as LF and checks it out however the
# platform wants. The working tree keeps behaving the way Windows expects; the
# repository stops carrying the question.
#
# This matters more here than in most projects. Void Palabra's entire claim is
# that two peers compute the same bytes for the same value — and a CR that
# wandered into a conformance vector would be a difference in the input to a
# hash, which is the one kind of difference this library is not allowed to have.

* text=auto

# ── FILES WHOSE ENDINGS ARE PART OF THEIR CONTRACT ──────────────────────────
# No shell scripts in the tree today. The rule is here anyway, because the first
# one added will be executed by bash, and a CR after a `then` or a heredoc
# terminator is a syntax error rather than a cosmetic problem.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# ── EXPLICIT TEXT, so nothing here is ever guessed at ────────────────────────
*.c         text
*.h         text
*.cpp       text
*.hpp       text
*.inc       text
*.py        text
*.md        text
*.txt       text
*.json      text
*.cmake     text
CMakeLists.txt text

# The conformance vectors are the contract (SPEC.md §9). They are plain JSON and
# must stay diffable, because a reviewer reading a changed expectation is the
# last line of defence against regenerating a failure away.
conformance/cases/*.json text diff

# ── BINARY, never touched, never diffed as text ─────────────────────────────
# Nothing binary is committed today — this library is source and vectors, and
# `vendor/` is cJSON's two source files rather than a prebuilt archive. Listed
# so that the first image or prebuilt artifact added is not line-ending mangled
# on the way in.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.woff2     binary
*.a         binary
*.lib       binary
*.dll       binary
*.exe       binary
*.o         binary
*.obj       binary
